{"tool_name":"chainer","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<blockquote>\n<p><em>Chainer</em>&nbsp;is a Python-based deep learning framework aiming at flexibility. It provides automatic differentiation APIs based on the&nbsp;<strong>define-by-run</strong>&nbsp;approach (a.k.a. dynamic computational graphs) as well as object-oriented high-level APIs to build and train neural networks. It also supports CUDA/cuDNN using&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/cupy/cupy\">CuPy</a>&nbsp;for high performance training and inference. For more details of Chainer, see the documents and resources listed above and join the community in Forum, Slack, and Twitter.</p>\n</blockquote>","summary":"","value":"<blockquote>\r\n<p><em>Chainer</em>&nbsp;is a Python-based deep learning framework aiming at flexibility. It provides automatic differentiation APIs based on the&nbsp;<strong>define-by-run</strong>&nbsp;approach (a.k.a. dynamic computational graphs) as well as object-oriented high-level APIs to build and train neural networks. It also supports CUDA/cuDNN using&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/cupy/cupy\">CuPy</a>&nbsp;for high performance training and inference. For more details of Chainer, see the documents and resources listed above and join the community in Forum, Slack, and Twitter.</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2025-10-27T01:28:03+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2018-06-04T13:13:43+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[{"cid":null,"comment_count":null,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":null,"last_comment_uid":null,"status":2}],"free_tagging":[{"target_id":4372,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"564b5f0b-e429-40c8-acbc-2ee6bcb29616","url":"/taxonomy/term/4372"},{"target_id":4388,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"09a4ce1a-d7bb-4ce4-8dfd-5fc9064e9ac2","url":"/taxono